body:
The frozen offset calculation has a redundant conditional check. Since `columns.slice(0, index)` already limits the iteration to columns before the current index, the `if (i < frozenColumns)` check inside the reduce is redundant for frozen columns (where index is always < frozenColumns). This check will always be true for frozen columns. Consider simplifying to: `columns.slice(0, index).reduce((sum, c) => sum + (typeof w === 'number' ? w : w ? parseInt(String(w), 10) || 150 : 150), selectable ? 48 : 0)`. Additionally, consider memoizing these offset calculations to avoid recalculating on every render, especially for tables with many columns.
```suggestion
                  ? columns.slice(0, index).reduce((sum, c) => {
                      const w = columnWidths[c.accessorKey] || c.width;
                      return sum + (typeof w === 'number' ? w : w ? parseInt(String(w), 10) || 150 : 150);
```
